WEBVTT

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.270
So you've arrived...

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.290
Lupin III.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:23.660
I could hardly dawdle after
being summoned, Countess.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.930
So how about you put that scary thing away?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.420
I need you to do something for me.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.610
Your reward will be this ring.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.600
You've shown up here time and time again, 
trying to get your hands on it.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.920
And every time...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.140
Well, shoot. You even held on 
to the pics to rub my nose in it.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.640
But isn't this ring 
a Maunbassant family heirloom?

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.580
Not to mention, a memento of your beloved?

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.830
Three years ago, my husband, Philippe, was shot 
and killed by an unknown assailant in Paris.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:00.970
I heard the police got nowhere with their 
inquiries, and it ended up as a cold case.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.070
Which is why I've continued 
investigating the matter privately.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.860
And now, I'm on the verge 
of discovering his killer.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:14.540
I've whittled it down to three suspects,
but it's still unclear which one of them did it.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.020
Your guests will be arriving shortly, ma'am.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.010
I see.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.870
I've invited the three of them here.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.280
I want you to figure out which 
one is my husband's killer.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.120
Aw, come on. You gotta be kidding me.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.950
<b>Introducing 
Detective Jim Barnett III</b>

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.940
<i>Count Philippe de Maunbassant.</i>

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.450
<i>The man who, in one generation, built
 the security systems industry in France.</i>

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.210
<i>No one could deny his brilliance,</i>

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.980
<i>and there were rumors that 
his business was set to go global...</i>

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.700
<i>But three years ago, while out 
jogging in a park in Paris,</i>

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.740
<i>someone took out a gun and shot him.</i>

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.090
<i>The world-famous sommelier, 
Frederik Autorett.</i>

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.450
<i>Renowned for his collection of gemstones,</i>

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:41.030
<i>he'd apparently been trying to pressure 
the count into selling him his emerald.</i>

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.360
<i>The count's nephew, Allan Dubois.</i>

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.960
<i>His father had a business that went to the wall,</i>

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.760
<i>and after the count refused to help, 
he committed suicide.</i>

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.630
<i>His family fell apart as a result.</i>

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.880
<i>Allan supposedly held a grudge against 
the count over what happened.</i>

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.610
<i>These days, he's a successful investor.</i>

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.890
<i>Pierre Schmidt.</i>

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.070
<i>Used to run a company that 
developed security systems tech,</i>

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.800
<i>but it was bought out by the 
count, and he was let go.</i>

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.110
<i>His subsequent business ventures 
didn't get off the ground,</i>

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:23.150
<i>so he currently ekes out a meager 
living as a computer repairman.</i>

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.250
You think the killer is 
one of these three men?

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.400
I'm sure of it.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.670
The cops aren't <i>totally</i> useless.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.910
They must have checked 'em out, right?

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.660
Yes, indeed. And all three had alibis.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.540
That rather tied their hands, I suppose.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.610
Which is why I've set a trap.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.680
The killer apparently tried to prize 
my husband's ring from his finger.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.820
But before he could get it, he panicked 
and fled, because a crowd was gathering.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:59.660
I've used a newly-developed chemical 
to isolate the DNA on the emerald.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.650
Really?!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:01.730
No, I made it up.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.810
It's a lie?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.050
But the killer will panic 
and try to cover his tracks.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:11.670
That's when I'd like you 
to apprehend him, Lupin.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:16.070
Good grief. I've got myself mixed up 
in a real headache of a situation this time.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.550
After showing everyone to their rooms,

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.160
tell them to assemble in the 
dining hall in an hour.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.190
Very good, ma'am.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.710
The balcony's on the brink of collapse,

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.430
so I've made sure the doors 
leading to it are all locked.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.180
It seems I'm not the only one 
who has grown fragile with age.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:43.410
This is actually a pretty bold scheme.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.930
The killer might try and 
come after you, y'know?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.940
I wouldn't worry.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.040
This is NZ Face.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.330
The world's first commercial 
facial recognition system.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.160
If anyone who isn't authorized tries to 
enter the castle, an alarm will sound.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.940
Does that include me?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.330
You're in the system.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.780
There's also a metal detector 
by the front door.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.560
Weapons are, of course, not allowed in here.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.970
One question, though. Why me?

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:23.430
Creating a system you couldn't 
circumvent was my husband's dream.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.980
He kept a scrapbook of clippings
 to record every time you made the news.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.750
At some point, he genuinely 
became a fan of yours.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.990
Which is why I believed you'd 
be the right man for the job.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.750
Well? Is that a satisfying answer?

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:43.260
Now... let's begin.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.540
I'm terribly sorry for making you wait.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.400
You called me here out of 
the blue. What's all this about?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.650
Not to mention, you haven't provided us 
with a meal, or even a glass of wine...

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.590
I beg your forgiveness.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.770
Marie is the only one of my help present 
today, so I'm a little shorthanded.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.120
Oh, is that so?

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.410
Wait, does that mean there's no food?

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.730
More importantly, 
I wanted to show you all this.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:27.080
You remember what happened 
three years ago, I trust?

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.760
I figured as much.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.260
The three of us are all suspects 
in the count's murder.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.600
I'm getting outta here.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.790
You're running away?

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.530
Th-That's not what I...

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:42.280
Your business got bought out, and now,
 you're just some two-bit repairman.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.690
I can only imagine how 
much that must piss you off.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.840
I was drinking in my usual bar at the time.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.270
One of the regulars confirmed it.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:52.310
Anyway, weren't you the one who 
was after the count's emerald?

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.030
I was partying at a hotel!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.780
I have an alibi, too!

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:59.300
A hotel that was five minutes' walk 
from the scene of the crime...

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.240
And you were found in the wine 
cellar all by yourself, weren't you?

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.140
He practically signed your father's death 
warrant. You've got no right to accuse me!

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:09.840
And people testified that 
they saw you at the scene.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.200
I was in Sicily at the time.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:15.520
The police have verified that 
it was a case of mistaken identity.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.490
Why would someone with 
my fortune take such a stupid risk?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:22.500
Not that a washed-up drunk like 
you would ever understand that.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.550
What did you call me?!

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.810
There's no need for all these accusations.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.240
I have conclusive evidence that will reveal 
the identity of my husband's killer.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.730
The emerald itself will tell us everything.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.810
Traces of the killer's identity 
were left behind on it.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.200
Using a special chemical,
 I will isolate the DNA and—

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.290
Wh-What the...

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.200
A blackout?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.450
What was that?!

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:46.090
It sounded like a gunshot!

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.490
Damn it all...

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.870
It's fine... Lupin...

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.860
Find the killer...

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:59.840
Don't tell me... Was this
your intention all along?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:16.210
The castle is now sealed off till dawn.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:19.470
Use that time to find the killer...

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.680
Your reward is on the table.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.800
The case will open automatically at dawn...

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:30.630
The case even you couldn't open...

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.640
Isabelle?!

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:32.520
Madam!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.980
This is insane.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.670
The drawbridge is up.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.520
So we're trapped in this place?

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.130
I would ask you all to calm down.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.540
The castle's in lockdown and 
will remain that way till dawn.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.890
By order of the countess...

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:50.300
What?!

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.900
And who the hell are you?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.420
I'm Lu—

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:58.410
No. Jim Barnett. A private eye
 hired by the countess.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:01.650
First, I need to ask you all 
to let me body-search you.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.800
What?

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.100
What did you say?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.660
You're just some two-bit gumshoe!

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.660
I'm sure it goes without saying,

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.470
but including myself, there 
were only six people in the castle.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:12.000
The countess has been murdered.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.660
Which means someone 
in this room is the killer.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.240
<i>So question is, who killed the countess?</i>

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.950
So much for that...

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.250
The tapes were removed.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.980
Which means no security camera footage.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:42.700
But the facial recognition 
system is still active.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:48.260
So if anyone other than you, me, and our 
bloodthirsty trio was in here, it'd tell us...

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:49.280
Where are they, anyway?

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.170
Back in their rooms.

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.780
I've locked the door to the dining room,
 so no one can go in there.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:01.790
I can't believe I didn't anticipate 
her doing something like this.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.220
She looks so peaceful.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.130
Mr. Barnett, she must really trust you.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.250
<i>Just give me time, Isabelle.</i>

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.020
So the three of them were sat over there...

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.860
<i>A blackout, a flash of light, and a gunshot.</i>

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>The countess...</i>

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.140
<i>First, I need to find the weapon.</i>

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:28.400
<i>I searched all three of them, 
but no one had a gun on them.</i>

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.420
<i>So where's the murder weapon?</i>

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.520
Excuse me, Mr. Barnett...

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:37.920
How was the killer able to shoot 
the countess in the dark?

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:41.060
Her wheelchair is electronic.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.140
They must've used these lights 
to line up the shot.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.540
That's...

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:52.550
I tidied up before everyone 
entered the dining room...

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.980
I would have noticed if there 
was this much pollen on the floor.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.910
Did you close the curtains in the hallway?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:04.810
No...

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.570
I only closed the curtains 
in the dining room.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:29.810
You greeted all three, 
and showed them in, right?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.930
Yes.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.930
And they stayed in their rooms after that?

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.570
Frederik left his room.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.560
Did he now?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:40.150
I ran into him in the hallway near 
the stairs to the basement...

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.690
Can I help you?

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.580
I-I was hoping to take 
a look at your wine cellar...

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:48.660
I'm afraid I can't open the door 
without the countess's permission.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.530
Fair enough. Well, some other time, then.

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:53.370
I see.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.160
Then, you didn't see Allan or Pierre?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.620
Actually, I did see Allan in his room.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:04.790
When I was walking down 
the hallway, his door was ajar.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.170
So you can confirm that he was in his room?

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:11.100
Yes. He was staring out of the window.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.600
A bit like this.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.110
And Pierre?

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.160
Mr. Pierre never left his room.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.270
I see...

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:26.450
I'm sorry I can't be of more help.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.040
Nah...

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:34.210
Of course! I've got it!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:38.020
Marie, get everyone to 
come to the dining room.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.420
Where's Pierre?

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.250
Who knows?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.050
Yo!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.770
Sorry, I dozed off for a bit.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.010
Right, now that we're all here...

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.310
You've figured out who the killer is?

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.770
I know <i>exactly</i> who it is.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.130
Sounds like fun.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:09.530
I mean, they relieved us of all guns 
and knives when we entered the castle...

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.040
How could any of us have shot the countess?

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.540
A bullet had been fired 
from the countess's gun.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.810
But that's nonsense.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.090
When did you check the barrel 
of her gun before the shooting?

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.880
When I was in her room.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.720
Well, when the two of you came in here, 
we were all sitting down already.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.390
We couldn't have gone to 
her room to grab her gun.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.300
And that's not all...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:36.710
You searched each of us, 
but didn't find the murder weapon.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.300
How do you explain that?

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:42.380
First, the culprit removed the tapes 
recording the security camera footage.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:46.610
After that, he waited for the 
right time to cut the castle's power.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:52.630
In the darkness, he used the light from her 
wheelchair to line up his shot and fire...

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.580
...killing the countess.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.940
This is so stupid. No one 
could've managed all that.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:01.070
Not anyone here, anyway.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.360
You make a good point.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:06.580
None of the people in this room 
could have carried out the murder.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.590
But there's no one else in the castle.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:13.210
I think this place has a facial recognition 
system that only lets in authorized people...

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:17.300
And if anyone else is detected, 
an alarm sounds.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.540
Well, in that case...

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:20.290
If you'd turn your 
attention to the flowers.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.680
You'll note that the rug 
underneath is covered in pollen.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:27.380
Apparently, this wasn't the case 
before you gentlemen showed up.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.860
What does that matter? It doesn't take much 
to make flowers spread their pollen!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.770
You're right. Accidentally brushing 
past could have caused it.

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.940
But question is, who would've 
brushed past the flowers?

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.480
Considering the amount of pollen,

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.110
the person who did is bound 
to have some on his clothes.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:45.130
But none of you had pollen on your clothing.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.210
There's something else that's odd...

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.770
The curtains on this hallway window.

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:55.410
According to Marie, she only closed 
the curtains in the dining room,

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.880
and the rest were all still open.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:02.200
So why are they closed?

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:07.570
Would you get to the point?! No one gives a damn
about this nonsense with curtains and pollen!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.890
You seem dead set on accusing 
one of us three as the killer,

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:14.300
but how about listening to my theory?

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.160
Let's hear it, then.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.670
I don't know what kind of hotshot 
detective you're supposed to be,

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.410
but how could you forget the most 
suspicious person in the room?!

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:25.910
Yes, I mean you.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.470
You could've slipped away 
without the detective noticing,

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:31.410
grabbed the countess's gun and stealthily 
put it back where you got it from.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.420
The pollen and the curtain 
were both disturbed by you!

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:39.320
You did that to disrupt the investigation, 
and make it seem like one of us was the killer!

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:42.820
No... I would <i>never</i> kill the countess...

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:45.320
Probably hungry to get 
her hands on her fortune.

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:49.070
That's not true! She took me in 
when I had no family...

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.670
And in the darkness, you slipped behind us,

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.070
and shot the countess from across the table!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.840
No! I didn't... I would never...

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.070
It's all right, Marie.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.830
Take you gloves off and show them.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.330
Do you need me to help you? 
Can you manage on your own?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:12.340
Oh, uh, yes. If you would, Mr. Barnett.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:17.460
See, this is why the countess chose you 
out of all her staff to work tonight.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:20.480
I burnt my hands in an 
accident three days ago.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.600
Marie!

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.110
I'm sorry.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.840
She's not pulling any triggers in her state.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:30.640
Now, for my theory.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:34.000
Why was the hallway curtain drawn?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:42.880
The lightning flashes posed a problem 
for the killer. So he shut the curtain.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.480
But why the <i>hallway</i> curtain?

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.870
Plus, the door was closed the whole time.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:52.360
The killer was worried a flash would 
light up the room at an inopportune moment.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.760
The power outage...

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:58.130
Exactly. At that moment, 
we were in total darkness.

00:17:58.130 --> 00:17:59.750
The door was opened?

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:00.770
No way...

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:03.880
But we were all sitting down. 
Who could've opened it?

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.650
There was a fourth guest.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:12.060
But the castle's facial recognition system
should've stopped anyone else getting in!

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:15.820
And yet, there was one person
 who was able to.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:17.360
Isn't that right, Allan?

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:22.070
In your room, you stood in front of the window
 that opened out onto the balcony, yes?

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:24.570
What were you doing there?

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:28.100
There was a cabinet stopping 
that window from opening.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.240
So why did you bother moving it?

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:31.860
W-Well...

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.770
One more thing...

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:40.080
Your car's tires made hard work of driving 
through the mud on the way in, right?

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:44.400
Makes me wonder whether you had 
something heavy in your trunk.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:48.400
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:52.290
It's the same method you used 
to kill the count three years ago.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:57.860
You haven't answered my question yet, either.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.910
Why did you move the cabinet?

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.900
What difference does it make?!

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.160
I have an alibi!

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:08.660
Unfortunately for you, that alibi 
doesn't hold water anymore.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:13.100
The countess sacrificed herself
 to pinpoint the killer.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:16.170
And her plan worked perfectly.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.850
No...

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:31.430
Bro!

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.510
Bro?!

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:33.690
Twins?

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.700
Bro!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:41.410
Looks like the system isn't advanced enough 
to tell the difference between twins.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.350
Then, what I saw...

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.200
Yeah. It wasn't his reflection in the glass.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.220
It was the twins, facing each other.

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:55.140
Allan let his brother into the house 
after he got out of the trunk.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.730
Our father was superstitious. 
He thought twins were bad luck.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.370
So he put my brother up for adoption.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:04.310
After my father killed himself, 
and I was left penniless...

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:06.630
I bumped into him again through sheer luck.

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.090
And you plotted revenge.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.480
Mr. Barnett, I thought...

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:32.640
I can't imagine she'd wanna meet her hubby 
in the afterlife without this thing.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.130
Mr. Barnett...

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:39.040
I've taken a shine to the name, though. 
Maybe I'll open a detective agency, someday.

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.540
And I might just need a trusty 
assistant, when the time comes.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.490
Of course. I'd be glad to help!

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:18.480
What do you mean the 
hideout toilet is busted?

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:22.270
Well, whatever. Jigen, let me use yours.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.830
Yours isn't working, either?!

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:25.560
Damn, what the heck am I supposed to do?!

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:27.990
I drank a skinful last night.
 I dunno if I can hold it...

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:31.380
No good! I'm gonna sprout a leak! 
This is bad! Here it comes!

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:35.180
Wait, Fujiko, why are you here?! 
And Old Man Zenigata, too?!

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:37.910
Uh, why are you here?! 
How'd you even know where we were?!

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:40.210
Next time: Fujiko's Souvenir.

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:44.920
<b>Fujiko's Souvenir</b>

00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:43.780
Dammit! Why the hell isn't the toilet working?!
